# Original ASM

`CRUNCH.ASM` is the loop (intro, level init, player, monsters, bullet, maps, songs). `SPRITE.ASM` is sprite init/move/draw/erase. `RAND.ASM` is the PRNG. `TUNESLIB.ASM` is beeper songs. `TI-85.H` is ZShell/ROM API.

Known constants (do not “fix” without a decision):

- Playfield: 16×8 tiles, 8×8 pixels each (`scrwidth=16`, `levelsize=128`).
- Up to 21 monsters; one player; one bullet; sprite struct 6 bytes.
- Tile/actor IDs are the first bitmap row byte (`playerid`, `monsterid`, `treeid`, etc.).
- Game loop: `moveplayer` every pass; `movemonster` + `movebullet` when `frame == $0700`.
- Eight maps selected with `level & 7`.

Comment-out / skip calc-specific video and ZShell tricks in the port; keep game logic. Strings (`title`, `byebye`, …) are used verbatim on VIC.
